SUMMARY:The Treachery of Botany: Poisonous Garden Plants
DESCRIPTION:🌿 BEAUTY OR BANE? THE SECRET LIFE OF YOUR GARDEN 💀 Vibran
 t lavender and mauve blossoms sway in the breeze while butterflies dip and
  dance above. With every rustle of foliage\, delicate white buds flash in 
 the sunlight. It’s the ultimate dream landscape—an idyllic\, peaceful 
 sanctuary designed for pure relaxation. But look closer. Hidden within thi
 s botanical paradise\, unexpected danger might be lurking right in plain s
 ight. Is that vivid red berry harmless or a hazard? What secret is that un
 usual violet flower stalk hiding? Could your pet's favorite sunbathing spo
 t be surrounded by toxic greenery? Uncover the truth behind the beauty! Jo
 in speakers Cynthia Trussell\, Indigo Bowser\, and Kathy Vu of the Penn St
 ate Master Gardeners for The Treachery of Botany: Poisonous Garden Plants.
  In this eye-opening 45-minute presentation (followed by a Q&A session)\, 
 you'll learn how to identify ordinary\, uncommon\, cultivated\, and wild p
 oisonous plants in your landscape-- discover what makes them tick\, and ma
 ster easy\, practical ways to manage them safely. Keep your loved ones saf
 e while keeping your sanctuary gorgeous. Don't miss it-- turn your garden 
 into a true\, worry-free paradise!\n\nPrice: Free\n\nSchedule listed: Mon\
 , Oct 26\, 2026 06:00 PM EDT – Mon\, Oct 26\, 2026 07:45 PM EDT\n\nSched
